=== P4: at MATCHED affinity, what depth can each element reach?
  Schloegl's A = 2.3979; the AM with the same affinity has gamma = exp(-A/3) = 0.4496
    AM      : delta* = 0.4018  ->  D_max = 33.5   (and no drive can push past 9.498e+09)
    Schloegl: lambda =  0.25, Delta = 0.1250  ->  D_max = 1   at the SAME affinity 2.3979
    Schloegl: lambda =  1.00, Delta = 0.5000  ->  D_max = 289.5   at the SAME affinity 2.3979
    Schloegl: lambda =  4.00, Delta = 2.0000  ->  D_max =   >1e18   at the SAME affinity 2.3979
    Schloegl: lambda = 16.00, Delta = 8.0000  ->  D_max =   >1e18   at the SAME affinity 2.3979
    Schloegl: lambda = 64.00, Delta = 32.0000  ->  D_max =   >1e18   at the SAME affinity 2.3979
  -> P4 HOLDS: at fixed affinity Schloegl passes AMs absolute ceiling; the currencies differ

=== P5 GUARD: does any of this survive re-expressing sigma as a fraction?
  Under sigma = f*Delta, Delta/sigma = 1/f identically, so D_max is the SAME for
  every element and every Delta -- the question cannot even be posed. That is why
  the fixed-sigma convention is the one used above, and why §12/§71/§72's matched
  predictions across substrates carried no information about the elements.

